 The `[payload.adt]` keys are passed to the ADT tool. The tool contract is device specific. The generic keys are documented in [Device tree](/porting/device-tree).
 
+## Patches of another source line
+
+The patches in `patches/xnu/` are written for the XNU version the base `feeds.toml` pins. A board
+that pins another line through its own `feeds.toml` supplies `patches/xnu-<major>/`, the overlay
+of that line:
+
+- `<name>.patch` replaces `patches/xnu/<name>.patch` and is applied in its place, so the base
+  order is kept.
+- `skip.txt` names base patches the line does not have, one `name: reason` per line. The build
+  prints every skip and refuses a name that the base tree no longer carries, so an omission
+  cannot silently outlive its patch.
+- A patch in the overlay without a base counterpart adds to the line.
+
+`kits/NativePrelink/patches/` is gated by file name instead: `xnu-<version>-*.patch` applies only
+when the pinned version matches.
+
 ## Defconfig
 
 `configs/<name>_defconfig` uses the same syntax as a Linux defconfig:
